- Auto loan FAQs

## Auto loan Frequently Asked Questions

Get the answers you need about Wells Fargo vehicle financing and servicing.

## Getting started

Wells Fargo auto loans are only available through our nationwide network of nearly 11,000 dealerships. Be sure to ask your dealership if Wells Fargo auto financing is available. If your loan is funded by Wells Fargo Auto, we''ll service your account.

We don''t offer refinancing for auto loans at this time. If you''re experiencing financial challenges, visit Help with auto loan payments to learn what options may be available to you.

Start by setting up your account . You''ll need your Social Security number and date of birth to get started. Once you have a username and password, you can use the Wells Fargo Mobile app or Wells Fargo Online® to make one-time payments, set up Autopay, access online statements, or manage other Wells Fargo accounts.

Your 10-digit auto loan account number can be found in the following places:

Welcome letter Your account number is provided with the loan details in the welcome letter that you receive in the mail after your new loan is funded.', ARRAY['Esta página solo está disponible en inglés', 'Popular FAQs']::text[], '## Popular FAQs

- Auto loan FAQs', NULL, false, 288, '1.3.0', '39a9c606-ce97-4a13-9c31-08e8ce063ec8', '9a76da8a-4934-4a60-838d-ca2bf689bd38', '2026-08-24 01:59:16.145233+00:00', '2026-08-24 01:59:16.145233+00:00', false, '');
