INSERT INTO "askcontent"."askcontent_document_chunk" ("connector_id", "document_id", "chunk_id", "ordinal", "text", "heading_path", "parent_text", "page", "is_table", "token_estimate", "chunker_version", "id", "org_id", "created_at", "updated_at", "is_code", "overlap") VALUES ('cba28334-247d-442a-bf39-8e6b4f466897', '6792a6d7-2a0b-4319-bd34-5f7ed047c449', 'chk_d00782e7c89c51b9', 32, '## Vehicle insurance

As stated in your loan contract, you''re required to maintain insurance on your vehicle throughout the duration of the loan. Your insurance policy must name Wells Fargo Auto as the loss payee.

Yes. You''re responsible for making your regular monthly payments until the loan is paid off. You should contact your insurance company to begin the claim process.

If you have Guaranteed Asset Protection (GAP) coverage on your loan, and your vehicle is a total loss, your loan balance or a portion of the balance, may be covered after the insurance settlement is applied.

There are a few options available:

- You can take the check to a Wells Fargo branch and ask an employee to endorse it on behalf of Wells Fargo Auto. Find a Wells Fargo banking location near you.

- You can mail us the check, which we''ll endorse, and then we''ll send the check back to you: Wells Fargo Auto Attn: Insurance Repairs MAC S3930-02D 2850 S Price Rd. Chandler, AZ 85286', ARRAY['Auto loan FAQs', 'Vehicle insurance']::text[], '## Vehicle insurance

As stated in your loan contract, you''re required to maintain insurance on your vehicle throughout the duration of the loan. Your insurance policy must name Wells Fargo Auto as the loss payee.

Yes. You''re responsible for making your regular monthly payments until the loan is paid off. You should contact your insurance company to begin the claim process.

If you have Guaranteed Asset Protection (GAP) coverage on your loan, and your vehicle is a total loss, your loan balance or a portion of the balance, may be covered after the insurance settlement is applied.

There are a few options available:

- You can take the check to a Wells Fargo branch and ask an employee to endorse it on behalf of Wells Fargo Auto. Find a Wells Fargo banking location near you.

- You can mail us the check, which we''ll endorse, and then we''ll send the check back to you: Wells Fargo Auto Attn: Insurance Repairs MAC S3930-02D 2850 S Price Rd. Chandler, AZ 85286

- If you''d like the insurance repair funds to be applied directly to your principal balance, endorse the check, and then mail it to us: Wells Fargo Auto Attn: Insurance Payments PO Box 842827 Los Angeles, CA 90084-2827 Or overnight to: Lockbox Services 842827 Wells Fargo Auto Attn: Insurance Payments 3440 Flair Dr. El Monte, CA 91731', NULL, false, 242, '1.3.0', 'b0e5cd87-c26f-479b-905d-109d1384f5e2', '9a76da8a-4934-4a60-838d-ca2bf689bd38', '2026-08-24 01:59:16.145233+00:00', '2026-08-24 01:59:16.145233+00:00', false, '');
INSERT INTO "askcontent"."askcontent_document_chunk" ("connector_id", "document_id", "chunk_id", "ordinal", "text", "heading_path", "parent_text", "page", "is_table", "token_estimate", "chunker_version", "id", "org_id", "created_at", "updated_at", "is_code", "overlap") VALUES ('cba28334-247d-442a-bf39-8e6b4f466897', '6792a6d7-2a0b-4319-bd34-5f7ed047c449', 'chk_0718fc61e788d18e', 33, '- If you''d like the insurance repair funds to be applied directly to your principal balance, endorse the check, and then mail it to us: Wells Fargo Auto Attn: Insurance Payments PO Box 842827 Los Angeles, CA 90084-2827 Or overnight to: Lockbox Services 842827 Wells Fargo Auto Attn: Insurance Payments 3440 Flair Dr. El Monte, CA 91731', ARRAY['Auto loan FAQs', 'Vehicle insurance']::text[], '## Vehicle insurance

As stated in your loan contract, you''re required to maintain insurance on your vehicle throughout the duration of the loan. Your insurance policy must name Wells Fargo Auto as the loss payee.

Yes. You''re responsible for making your regular monthly payments until the loan is paid off. You should contact your insurance company to begin the claim process.

If you have Guaranteed Asset Protection (GAP) coverage on your loan, and your vehicle is a total loss, your loan balance or a portion of the balance, may be covered after the insurance settlement is applied.

There are a few options available:

- You can take the check to a Wells Fargo branch and ask an employee to endorse it on behalf of Wells Fargo Auto. Find a Wells Fargo banking location near you.

- You can mail us the check, which we''ll endorse, and then we''ll send the check back to you: Wells Fargo Auto Attn: Insurance Repairs MAC S3930-02D 2850 S Price Rd. Chandler, AZ 85286

- If you''d like the insurance repair funds to be applied directly to your principal balance, endorse the check, and then mail it to us: Wells Fargo Auto Attn: Insurance Payments PO Box 842827 Los Angeles, CA 90084-2827 Or overnight to: Lockbox Services 842827 Wells Fargo Auto Attn: Insurance Payments 3440 Flair Dr. El Monte, CA 91731', NULL, false, 83, '1.3.0', 'ca9169e9-ce7f-46ac-ba37-082df52d4d8a', '9a76da8a-4934-4a60-838d-ca2bf689bd38', '2026-08-24 01:59:16.145233+00:00', '2026-08-24 01:59:16.145233+00:00', false, 'which we''ll endorse, and then we''ll send the check back to you: Wells Fargo Auto Attn: Insurance Repairs MAC S3930-02D 2850 S Price Rd. Chandler, AZ 85286');
INSERT INTO "askcontent"."askcontent_document_chunk" ("connector_id", "document_id", "chunk_id", "ordinal", "text", "heading_path", "parent_text", "page", "is_table", "token_estimate", "chunker_version", "id", "org_id", "created_at", "updated_at", "is_code", "overlap") VALUES ('cba28334-247d-442a-bf39-8e6b4f466897', '6792a6d7-2a0b-4319-bd34-5f7ed047c449', 'chk_184390e977d2a214', 34, '## Aftermarket products

Aftermarket products are optional products or services that may be purchased from the dealership along with your vehicle. Some examples include:

- Guaranteed Asset Protection (GAP) covers all or a portion of the loan balance after the payment of a total loss insurance claim.

- Service contracts (also referred to as extended warranties) provide coverage if a major mechanical component of the vehicle, such as an engine, transmission, heating/cooling system, seal, gasket, and/or fuel system, needs repair. The coverage typically lasts for a specific period or vehicle mileage.

- Anti-theft protection includes devices or services, such as tracking, that make the vehicle (or the component of the vehicle) more difficult to steal or easier to recover if it''s stolen. It can also provide a financial benefit after a theft.

- Surface protection for the interior or exterior of the vehicle.', ARRAY['Auto loan FAQs', 'Aftermarket products']::text[], '## Aftermarket products

Aftermarket products are optional products or services that may be purchased from the dealership along with your vehicle. Some examples include:

- Guaranteed Asset Protection (GAP) covers all or a portion of the loan balance after the payment of a total loss insurance claim.

- Service contracts (also referred to as extended warranties) provide coverage if a major mechanical component of the vehicle, such as an engine, transmission, heating/cooling system, seal, gasket, and/or fuel system, needs repair. The coverage typically lasts for a specific period or vehicle mileage.

- Anti-theft protection includes devices or services, such as tracking, that make the vehicle (or the component of the vehicle) more difficult to steal or easier to recover if it''s stolen. It can also provide a financial benefit after a theft.

- Surface protection for the interior or exterior of the vehicle.

- Maintenance packages are prepaid plans that typically cover scheduled maintenance, such as oil changes, on the vehicle.

Once we receive the primary insurance settlement from your insurance company, we''ll work with the dealership and the product administrators to determine if any aftermarket products you financed are refundable. We''ll issue a refund to you for any eligible aftermarket product refunds as follows:

- If your account balance is zero, we''ll send you a check.

- If you have an account balance, we''ll apply the refund to your principal balance. Note: The refund won''t apply toward your monthly payment and won''t reduce your monthly payment amount. However, the refund to your principal balance may reduce the amount of interest you pay, and it may help you pay off your loan more quickly than the original term.

- If your loan originated in the state of Nevada, we won’t apply the refund to your principal balance for non-GAP products. We’ll send you a check for the aftermarket product refund instead.

This is a personal decision for you to make based on your needs. When deciding to buy an aftermarket product, consider the cost, what is covered and excluded, how long the coverage lasts, and how you plan to use the vehicle. The purchase of aftermarket products is optional and isn''t required to receive approval for your loan.

Contact the dealership where you purchased your vehicle, or the coverage provider, for more information. If you need a copy of the aftermarket product contract, call us at 1-800-289-8004 .

The contract for the aftermarket product will provide specific details of the coverage. If you have questions, contact the dealership where you purchased your vehicle. The dealer can best explain the aftermarket product, what''s covered, and how it works. If you still have questions after you contact the dealership, or if you need a copy of the aftermarket product contract, call us at 1-800-289-8004 .

Contact the dealership where you purchased your vehicle and request a signed copy of the aftermarket product contract. All purchased products require a signature. If the dealer is unable to provide a signed copy, call us at 1-800-289-8004 .

If your vehicle is under warranty, or if you purchased a service contract, your vehicle may be covered. Review the terms of your warranty or service contract, as applicable, or contact the service contract provider for more information.

If your vehicle isn''t under warranty, and you didn''t purchase a service contract, contact your local dealership to determine other repair options.

Contact the coverage provider for information about filing a claim or using the product. The coverage prov', NULL, false, 229, '1.3.0', '8b4fd3d9-fb94-408d-81bc-53110016600b', '9a76da8a-4934-4a60-838d-ca2bf689bd38', '2026-08-24 01:59:16.145233+00:00', '2026-08-24 01:59:16.145233+00:00', false, '');
