To find your full account and routing numbers in your account online, simply sign on to Wells Fargo Online ® and select the account you’re interested in. Then, follow these instructions:

## Account number

To access your full account number, select Account and the 4 numbers directly below the account name.', ARRAY['Routing Numbers and Account Numbers', 'View online']::text[], '## View online

To find your full account and routing numbers in your account online, simply sign on to Wells Fargo Online ® and select the account you’re interested in. Then, follow these instructions:', NULL, false, 81, '1.3.0', 'c3cd2c01-bade-4df3-b22d-4aba0749b778', '9a76da8a-4934-4a60-838d-ca2bf689bd38', '2026-08-24 01:59:16.145233+00:00', '2026-08-24 01:59:16.145233+00:00', false, '');
INSERT INTO "askcontent"."askcontent_document_chunk" ("connector_id", "document_id", "chunk_id", "ordinal", "text", "heading_path", "parent_text", "page", "is_table", "token_estimate", "chunker_version", "id", "org_id", "created_at", "updated_at", "is_code", "overlap") VALUES ('cba28334-247d-442a-bf39-8e6b4f466897', '6792a6d7-2a0b-4319-bd34-5f7ed047c449', 'chk_4678e6fc4cfe30f5', 42, '## Guaranteed Asset Protection (GAP) coverage

GAP is an optional product that covers any "gap" between the amount owed on the loan and the vehicle''s value in the event of a total loss. Some exclusions apply. It''s important to review the coverage details to understand the limitations of GAP coverage.

No, GAP coverage only helps in the event of a total loss and is considered a supplement to your primary insurance. Auto insurance covers the vehicle, while GAP covers the loan.

GAP applies to a specific loan and isn''t transferable. If you''d like GAP coverage on your new loan, you''ll need to purchase a new GAP product.

If you pay off your loan early, or if the vehicle has been repossessed and sold, we''ll initiate cancellation of your GAP product. We''ll either send you the refund for any unused portion (if your account balance is zero) or apply the refund to your principal balance. Refund processing time may take up to 120 days. Note: Some GAP products may not be eligible for a refund. Review your GAP contract to confirm eligibility.', ARRAY['Auto loan FAQs', 'Guaranteed Asset Protection (GAP) coverage']::text[], '## Guaranteed Asset Protection (GAP) coverage

GAP is an optional product that covers any "gap" between the amount owed on the loan and the vehicle''s value in the event of a total loss. Some exclusions apply. It''s important to review the coverage details to understand the limitations of GAP coverage.

No, GAP coverage only helps in the event of a total loss and is considered a supplement to your primary insurance. Auto insurance covers the vehicle, while GAP covers the loan.

GAP applies to a specific loan and isn''t transferable. If you''d like GAP coverage on your new loan, you''ll need to purchase a new GAP product.

If you pay off your loan early, or if the vehicle has been repossessed and sold, we''ll initiate cancellation of your GAP product. We''ll either send you the refund for any unused portion (if your account balance is zero) or apply the refund to your principal balance. Refund processing time may take up to 120 days. Note: Some GAP products may not be eligible for a refund. Review your GAP contract to confirm eligibility.

You should contact your insurance company to begin the auto insurance claim process.

If you have GAP and your vehicle is deemed a total loss or was stolen, we''ll initiate the GAP claim after the insurance settlement has posted to your account. We''ll send you a letter letting you know the GAP claim has started and stating whether further action is needed from you to complete the GAP claim. If you have any questions during this process, call us at 1-800-289-8004 .

If your vehicle has been sufficiently damaged, and if permitted by your GAP contract, you may be eligible to file a GAP claim despite not having insurance coverage. A claim may help cover a portion of the amount owed on your loan. You should consider contacting the GAP administrator, or the dealership where you purchased the vehicle, to see if you are eligible to file a GAP claim, or if it would be beneficial to cancel the GAP product and receive a refund for the unused portion, if applicable.

There are limitations and exclusions for GAP coverage, which you can find in the GAP contract. If you have questions about the coverage, contact the dealership or the coverage provider. If you need a copy of the GAP contract, contact the dealership or call us at 1-800-289-8004 .', NULL, false, 261, '1.3.0', 'e31a0f25-dd33-4daa-814a-902912850640', '9a76da8a-4934-4a60-838d-ca2bf689bd38', '2026-08-24 01:59:16.145233+00:00', '2026-08-24 01:59:16.145233+00:00', false, '');
